" Tridactyl config
" Location: ~/.config/tridactyl/tridactylrc  (symlinked from dotfiles)
" Tridactyl reads this file every time Firefox starts.
" To re-apply it without restarting:  :source   (or ,r below)

" ── 0. Reset ─────────────────────────────────────────────
" Wipe every setting Tridactyl has stored inside Firefox, then apply this file.
" Result: this file is the ONLY place your config lives.
" Anything you set by typing (:set, :bind, M<key>) is lost at the next
" restart unless you also write it here.
sanitise tridactyllocal tridactylsync

" ── 1. Behaviour ─────────────────────────────────────────
" Keys work by physical position, so they still work with the Russian layout on.
set keyboardlayoutforce true

" Stop pages from putting the cursor into a text box when they load.
" (Otherwise your keys type into that box instead of controlling Tridactyl.)
set allowautofocus false

" What :open / :tabopen search with when you type words instead of a URL.
set searchengine duckduckgo

" Needed so ",b" below doesn't auto-insert the first bookmark when you press space.
# set completions.Bmark.autoselect false

" ── 2. Appearance ────────────────────────────────────────
" Placeholder. Will be replaced with a theme matched to your Emacs theme.
colourscheme plaindark

" ── 3. Write in Emacs (optional) ─────────────────────────
" In any text box: press Ctrl-i, write in Emacs, save and close the frame,
" and the text goes back into the box.
" Needs a running Emacs server. Check the path with `which emacsclient`.
set editorcmd /opt/homebrew/bin/emacsclient -c

" ── 4. Common sites (quickmarks) ─────────────────────────
" Format:   quickmark <key> <url> [<url> ...]
" Open:     gn<key> new tab · go<key> current tab · gw<key> new window
" One key can hold several URLs; it then opens all of them (a "folder").
" Keys are single characters: a–z, A–Z, 0–9.
"
" (to be filled in once the site list is ready)

" ── 5. Own keybindings ───────────────────────────────────
" , is unused by Tridactyl's defaults, so it serves as a prefix for own binds.

" Search all bookmarks, open the chosen one in a new tab.
bind ,b fillcmdline bmarks -t

" Re-apply this file.
bind ,r source
